sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant EXT as Extension (CRX / source)
    participant RD as Isolated Reader
    participant SA as Static Analyzer (CoCo / DoubleX)
    participant OR as Orchestrator
    participant KB as Knowledge Base (Graph-RAG)
    participant AG as PoC Agents
    participant HN as Chrome MV3 Harness
    participant JG as Evidence Judge

    EXT->>RD: Source code and manifest
    RD->>RD: Unpack, parse, extract security facts
    RD->>SA: Components (cs / bg / manifest)

    alt tools_on (taint available)
        SA->>SA: CoCo + DoubleX taint path
        SA->>OR: Fact Sheet (findings + witness)
    else tools_off / incomplete analysis
        SA->>OR: Fact Sheet (candidate sinks from permissions)
    end

    OR->>OR: Triage (3 states) + mode select + attacker_entry gate

    loop Refinement (<= N iterations)
        alt anchor on finding (tools_on)
            OR->>KB: Query with structured finding
        else anchor on manifest (tools_off)
            OR->>KB: Query with manifest + attacker surface
        end
        KB-->>OR: API semantics, patterns, skeletons A/B, few-shot
        OR->>AG: Security hypothesis + constraints + trigger/message
        AG->>AG: Plan and generate candidate PoC (attacker model A/B)
        AG->>AG: PoC safety and scope validation (sandbox-only)
        AG->>OR: Candidate PoC + expected evidence (oracle)
        OR->>HN: Validated test package
        HN->>HN: Execute in isolated Chrome MV3 (attacker A/B)
        HN->>JG: Instrumented execution trace
        JG->>JG: Evaluate deterministic oracle + call-stack sanity
        JG-->>OR: Verdict and evidence
        OR->>OR: Revise (refiners) / stop / report
    end

    opt On confirmed PoC
        OR->>KB: Store verified PoC (closed loop to few-shot / skeletons)
    end
